Source: https://github.com/MesTTo/MeTTa-Library-Pack
License: Apache-2.0
Comment: Purpose: the licence of each file in this pack that is not the
 pack's own code alone, with the licence texts shipped beside it: the native
 halves under */support and the code they vendor, and every vendored or
 adapted Prolog and MeTTa file. tools/host-notices/notices.py in MesTTo/MeTTa
 reads it when the WebAssembly host links the halves each support/static.cmake
 names, and refuses a compiled file no paragraph here names, so the map has no
 `Files: *`: a new file in a half needs its own line before a host can ship
 it. extensions/python/tools/librarylicences.py in MesTTo/MeTTa derives each
 library's (package license) row from it: Apache-2.0, the pack's licence for
 its own code, and the licence of every paragraph naming a file of the
 library or a _support file its lib.metta imports; it refuses a file under a
 vendor/ directory that no paragraph names. tests/checks/check_notices_coverage.py
 in MesTTo/MeTTa holds every file of the halves the WebAssembly host stages to
 a paragraph, or to being a licence text one names.

